  "method": "Every figure is computed by the app's own engine; nothing is typed by hand. GRIHA PRAVESH: for every civil day of 2027 the panchang (computePanchanga) is read at local sunrise. A day is listed only when ALL hold: the Moon is in a griha pravesh nakshatra of RULES.griha_pravesh (app/lib/muhurat.ts: Rohini, Mrigashira, Pushya, Hasta, Anuradha, Revati, Uttara Phalguni, Uttara Ashadha, Uttara Bhadrapada); scoreDay(p, 'griha_pravesh') raises no warning (no avoid-nakshatra, no avoided tithi 4/8/9/14/Amavasya in either paksha, no Sunday/Tuesday/Saturday, no inauspicious yoga, no Vishti karana); and seasonalExclusionsFor('griha_pravesh', ...) from app/lib/muhurat-exclusions.ts is empty: Kharmas (Sun in Dhanu), Malmas (Sun in Meena), Chaturmas, adhik and kshaya maas, Shukra and Guru asta with 3 vriddha/bala days each side. A season excludes a day when any part of the sunrise-to-sunrise day is inside it (both sunrises are tested), the convention Drik Panchang prints as a partial overlap. This is the same filter (web/test/wedding-season-index-derivation.ts) the Wedding Season Index and the 2026 vivah report use for marriage, run with the griha_pravesh rules. Drik Panchang additionally restricts griha pravesh to six lunar months; the app does not, so this list is a superset of Drik's on that axis. INGRESSES and STATIONS: sidereal (Lahiri) longitudes through the Swiss Ephemeris wrapper, sampled daily at 00:00 IST and bisected to well under a minute; every crossing is verified one minute either side. Rahu is the mean node; Ketu is Rahu + 180 degrees. KHARMAS / MALMAS: the Sun's sidereal ingress instants, bisected the same way. An instant is a single astronomical moment shown in IST, not a city time.",
